Sure, here is a basic CSS for a loading spinner animation using only the `-webkit-animation` property. Please note this example uses what is known as the "doughnut" or "spinner" animation:

```css
@-webkit-keyframes spin {
  from {
    -webkit-transform: rotate(0deg);
  }
  to {
    -webkit-transform: rotate(360deg);
  }
}

.spinner {
  background-color: #ccc;
  width: 100px;
  height: 100px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  -webkit-animation: spin 1.5s infinite linear;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}
```

